n); 'Restructuring & other' is the rest of S&P Global's reported expenses ($9.2B) (calculated). Operating profit includes $273M of disposition gains and $28M of equity income. *Market Intelligence in the flow chart is net of $200M of intersegment eliminations.","Other figures are from S&P Global's Q4 2025 results (8-K). Total equity excludes about $4.9B of redeemable noncontrolling interest (mainly the S&P Dow Jones Indices partnership), so assets ≠ liabilities + equity in the bars. Free cash flow = operating cash flow − capex (calculated).","Percentages are of revenue; figures may not sum due to rounding."],"report":{"summary":["S&P Global's revenue rose 7.9% to $15.3B in 2025. Ratings grew 8.1% on strong debt issuance and Indices 13.6%, while Market Intelligence grew 5.8%. Operating profit rose 16.1% to $6.5B, a 42.2% margin.","Net income grew 16.1% to $4.5B, and EPS 18.7% to $14.66; adjusted EPS was $17.83. S&P Global bought back $5.0B of stock, nearly all of its $5.5B free cash flow, and plans to spin off its Mobility division in mid-2026."],"highlights":["Operating margin rose to 42.2%.","EPS rose 18.7% to $14.66.","Indices revenue grew 13.6%.","Buybacks rose 51.5% to $5.0B."],"watch":["Free cash flow fell 2.0%.","Total debt rose 14.8% to $13.1B.","Ratings depends on debt issuance.","Mobility spin-off adds one-time costs."],"table":[["Revenue",15.336,14.208,1],["Cost of revenue",4.563,4.361],["Gross profit",10.773,9.847,1],["Operating expenses",4.295,4.267],["Operating income",6.478,5.58,1],["Interest & other, net",-0.251,-0.272],["Income before taxes",6.227,5.308],["Income tax",1.407,1.141],["Net income to S&P Global",4.471,3.852,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",14.66,12.35,0,"eps"],["Operating cash flow",5.651,5.689],["Free cash flow",5.456,5.565,1]],"sources":[["S&P Global Q4 and full year 2025 results (SEC 8-K)","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/64040/000006404026000007/a4q2025earningsrelease.htm"],["StockAnalysis — S&P Global income statement","https://stockan